<%#
    The theme, for the <head> of every page.

    Included once per view, so the palette and the way to change it are defined in
    one place rather than repeated and drifting.

    THREE PARTS, each for a reason:

      1. The stylesheets. palette.css carries the 22 palettes as variables,
         app.css maps them onto semantic roles and holds the components.
      2. The inline script. The server sets data-theme from the cookie, so a
         stored choice is already correct on the first paint. For the
         system-preference case the server cannot know the OS setting, so this
         script reads it and picks the matching palette BEFORE the body is parsed.
         That is what keeps the flash off the screen rather than making it brief.
      3. Nothing here reads localStorage: the cookie is the one source of truth,
         which is why the server could render the right theme in the first place.
 
      THE COOKIE NOTICE IS INCLUDED FROM HERE, at the end, and that is the same reasoning as
      the picker above: it is site chrome rather than one page's content, and it must appear
      wherever the site does. It used to be inline in `admin-login.ejs`, so every other page
      rendered no banner at all - which the owner met as "not clickable", there being nothing
      to click. Nothing about the notice is page-specific: every page sets the same two
      cookies through this same include, so every page owes the reader the same notice.
%>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= basePath %>/css/palette.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= basePath %>/css/app.css">
<%# Page-specific sheets, so a page pays only for what it renders. %>
<% if (typeof pageStyles !== 'undefined') { %>
    <% pageStyles.forEach(function (sheet) { %>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= basePath %>/css/<%= sheet %>.css">
    <% }); %>
<% } %>
<script>
    // Runs before the body renders, so no frame is painted in the wrong theme.
    // Only needed when the choice is "follow system"; a stored palette is already
    // on <html> from the server.
    (function () {
        var FOLLOW = 'system';
        var root = document.documentElement;

        if (root.getAttribute('data-theme') !== FOLLOW) return;

        // The ids match lib/palettes.js: Catppuccin and Catppuccin Latte, the same
        // palette in the two modes.
        try {
            var dark = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
            root.setAttribute('data-theme', dark ? '<%= theme.systemDarkId %>' : '<%= theme.systemLightId %>');
        } catch (err) {
            // matchMedia unavailable: palette.css already applied the dark pair for
            // the "system" category, so there is a usable theme and nothing to do.
        }
    })();
</script>

<%- include('cookie-notice') %>
